  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1: 1 Uno, 1 breadboard, 1 pushbutton, 1 photoresistor, 2x 10k, 1x 220 ohm, 1 LED and 10 jumper wires.",
   "The schematic is followed for the electrical connections: 5V - photoresistor - A0 node - 10k - GND; 5V - button - pin 2 node - 10k - GND; pin 9 - 220 ohm - LED anode, LED cathode - GND.",
   "The breadboard picture is ambiguous about which side of the button the pin-2 wire and the 10k resistor sit on. I put the pin-2 wire and the button's 10k pull-down on the same side, the bottom half. The 5V side of the button is on the top half and is fed by a red jumper (wire6) from the top + rail. The photoresistor's 5V jumper (wire7) comes from the bottom + rail.",
   "The top rails are used as + (tp) and GND (tn), and the bottom rails as + (bp) and GND (bn). They are linked on the right by wire9 and wire10.",
   "Exact column numbers are my own placement, chosen to fit the image roughly. The text says 'analog input 2' but the image, schematic and code use A0.",
   "The 10k resistors are given as value=10000 (ohms)."
  ]
 },
